From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:22:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] perf(biome): reuse seasonal weather per biome in
 injectBiomeTemperature

Every World.getBiome call ran getSeasonWeather, which rebuilt the biome
id string for the force-snow list and allocated a Pair and a boxed
Float. getSeasonWeather only reads its arguments and the config, so
compute it once for all four seasons into an immutable per-biome table
keyed by the config instance, biome id and original weather (identity
and values), and rebuild the table whenever any of them differs. The
season is still resolved on every call and the same weather fields are
written, so the values seen by rendering, precipitation and spawning are
unchanged. A config-parameter overload keeps the public getSeasonWeather
signature and body; a null season keeps the original code path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
